    <statement><p>Evaluate the function at the specified points.</p>
<p><m>f(x,y) = y+xy^{4}, \left(-3,-1\right), \left(-2,1\right), \left(-5,-5\right)</m></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-3,-1\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-2,1\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>At <m>\left(-5,-5\right)</m>: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-3130</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>(x,y) = \left(-3,-1\right)</m> to find 
<m>f(-3,-1) = -1   - 3(-1)^{4} = -4</m>.



Similarly, with <m>(x,y) = \left(-2,1\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(-2,1) = 1   - 2(1)^{4} = -1</m>.



Finally, for <m>(x,y) = \left(-5,-5\right)</m> we find 
<m>f(-5,-5) = -5   - 5(-5)^{4} = -3130</m>.


</solution>
